{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "a8f3c2e1-4b5d-6e7f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b",
		"name": "Convocon — Bookings API",
		"description": "API collection for the Convocon Bookings module (Reminders).\n\n## Authentication\n\n**Public booking widgets** use a scoped **booking key** (`bk_…`) from Booking settings. Pass it as `booking_key` in the query string (GET) or JSON body (POST), or as the `X-Booking-Key` header. Do not put owner API tokens in public URLs.\n\n**Server integrations** may use a **Sanctum personal access token** belonging to the company owner. Pass it as `token` in the query string (GET) or JSON body (POST).\n\nGenerate an owner token via `php artisan tinker`:\n```php\n$user = \\App\\Models\\User::find(1);\n$user->createToken('bookings-api')->plainTextToken;\n```\n\n## Recommended booking flow\n1. **List services** — discover bookable services for the company.\n2. **Availability (dates)** — which calendar days have open slots.\n3. **Availability (slots)** — time slots for a chosen date; copy a `slot_id`.\n4. **Create reservation** — book using `slot_id` (validates capacity, staff, and rules).\n5. **Cancel / reschedule** — manage the reservation lifecycle.\n\n## Notes\n- `source` is a **bookable service** name or numeric ID (`is_bookable = true` in Bookings admin).\n- `slot_id` format: `{appointment_staff_id}|{ISO8601_UTC_start}|{duration_minutes}` — returned by the availability endpoints.\n- Booking creates or reuses a contact automatically; **you do not need** `POST /api/wpbox/makeContact` before booking.\n- Contacts created via booking may have `has_chat = 0` until promoted to the inbox (configurable in Booking settings).\n\n## Error responses\n| HTTP | Meaning |\n|------|----------|\n| 400 | Validation failed (`errors` object) |\n| 401 | Invalid or missing credentials |\n| 404 | Service or reservation not found |\n| 409 | Slot no longer available |\n| 422 | Invalid booking payload (e.g. bad `slot_id`) |",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
